5. Security & Access Architecture
Authentication: Handled by Firebase Authentication. Offloading password hashing, MFA, and OAuth (Google Workspace for Education) to Google ensures enterprise-grade identity security.

Authorization (RBAC):

SuperAdmin (Attendora Platform Owners)

TenantAdmin (College Principals / IT)

Teacher (Can mark/edit attendance for assigned subjects)

Student (Read-only access to own records)

Secret Management: Environment variables injected via deployment platform (e.g., Render/AWS Secrets Manager). No secrets in code.

Data in Transit: TLS 1.3 mandated at the Edge.

Audit Logging: Any modification to past attendance records or changes in user roles generates an immutable audit log entry in the database containing: timestamp, user_id, tenant_id, action, previous_state, new_state.

